WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.825
The orphan rule becomes a plan,
and nothing in the plan writes.

2
00:00:03.825 --> 00:00:08.700
Each orphan candidate and each
claim turns into exactly one action.

3
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:12.669
Most are bookkeeping: waiting
for the officer's confirmation,

4
00:00:12.669 --> 00:00:16.171
a claim window still open, an
exception with an end date,

5
00:00:16.171 --> 00:00:19.362
or a retirement candidate
once the window closes.

6
00:00:19.362 --> 00:00:23.194
Only two actions ever write:
disabling a confirmed orphan,

7
00:00:23.194 --> 00:00:25.588
and adding an owner someone claimed.

8
00:00:25.588 --> 00:00:26.924
Here's the clever part.

9
00:00:26.924 --> 00:00:30.585
The same inputs always give
the same plan, byte for byte,

10
00:00:30.585 --> 00:00:33.513
so a reviewer doesn't
approve a description.

11
00:00:33.513 --> 00:00:34.920
They approve a hash.
